<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Han Xin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 196 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Han Xin was the leading general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> in the Chu–Han war that founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>. Having deserted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a>, he took the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> heartland in 206 BCE, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-bao">Wei Bao</a> in 205 BCE by crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> on rafts, conquered Zhao and Qi, and made himself King of Qi in 203 BCE. He helped destroy Xiang Yu at Gaixia in 202 BCE, but was demoted and executed for alleged treason in 196 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/han-xin.jpg" alt="Han Xin" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B1%89%E6%B7%AE%E9%98%B4%E4%BE%AF%E9%9F%A9%E4%BF%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
